## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class bears `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4** (of 7)   |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 93–109)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means one branch is never exercised — the test always passes but only half the logic is verified. Integration-test calibration does **not** exempt Conditional Test Logic.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — if the runtime type changes, the untested branch silently becomes the live path.

---

#### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** No assertion — test passes even if every insert silently drops data. Framework reports it green as long as no exception is thrown.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage metrics look good but nothing is actually verified.

---

#### ❸ Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High; integration calibration applied)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82–90)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hard-coded 3-second wall-clock delay. Makes the suite slower, introduces non-determinism (may flake on slow CI agents), and the delay is a magic number with no documented rationale.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var notified = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(notified, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI and an unconditional 3 s penalty per run.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–39)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, zero message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output shows only the expected/actual values — you must read the code to understand *which property* was wrong.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis; trivial to fix but compounds as the suite grows.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✓

The remaining 3 tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's clean |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, single assertion |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate concurrency scenario with a clear count assertion |

`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` also passes cleanly — `Assert.AreEqual(3, users.Count)` is contextually obvious (3 items inserted on the preceding lines) and correctly **not** flagged as a Magic Number.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add count assertion to `BulkInsert` | ~2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into 2 tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling helper | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to multi-assert tests | ~5 min |

Fixes 1 and 2 prevent **false passes** — they should be addressed immediately. Fixes 3–4 improve reliability and diagnostics.
